        "original_id": "4aa3a155-eb58-5b4a-bb73-b6eb0f493766",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Films: Winnie the Pooh (2011 film), Rudyard Kipling's The Jungle Book (1994 film)\n- People: Stephen Sommers, Edward S. Feldman, Raju Patel, Ronald Yanover, Mark Geldman, Travis Oates, Jim Cummings\n- Companies: Walt Disney Animation Studios, Walt Disney Pictures, Sisu Auto\n- Organizations: Finnish Army\n- Products: Nasu, Nauha-Sisu\n\nFacts:\n- Rudyard Kipling's The Jungle Book is a 1994 American live-action adventure film co-written and directed by Stephen Sommers.\n- Rudyard Kipling's The Jungle Book was produced by Edward S. Feldman and Raju Patel from a story by Ronald Yanover and Mark Geldman.\n- Winnie the Pooh is a 2011 American animated buddy musical comedy film produced by Walt Disney Animation Studios and released by Walt Disney Pictures.\n- Travis Oates and Jim Cummings were the only two original voice actors to return for the 2011 Winnie the Pooh movie.\n- The Nasu, also called Nauha-Sisu and meaning \"Piglet\" in Finnish, is a tracked articulated all-terrain transport vehicle.\n- Sisu Auto developed the Nasu for the Finnish Army.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
